On the show today:

CBS News fires self-aggrandizing agitprop host Scott Pelley for insubordination, and the Left goes crazy;

we review election results from across the country… and examine the Left’s civil war;

and Megyn Kelly and Shawn Ryan demonstrate that the Woke Right is just the New Left.

open.spotify.com/episode/18J…

On the show today:

A shocking stabbing in the UK lights the internet on fire – and raises questions about the weaponization of tolerance;

Hasan Piker and Cenk Uygur find themselves on the outs with the British government;

and Pride Month is back with a vengeance.

open.spotify.com/episode/6yP…

On the show today:

Maine Senate Democratic candidate Graham Platner’s campaign hits the skids after it turns out he was sexting up to a dozen women while married;

party Democrats show that there’s no such thing as a Republican moderate enough for them to vote for him;

and Los Angeles prepares to pick a mayor.

open.spotify.com/episode/7vk…

On the show today:

I'm going to say a bunch of stuff that will piss off the internet about free markets and Jeff Bezos;

Democrats won't stop defending extremism;

and New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani wants to be a streamer.

open.spotify.com/episode/5yZ…

On the show today:

Thomas Massie goes down in flames in the most expensive House primary ever… and we examine just what happened to the seven-term Congressman;

President Trump endorses Ken Paxton over Senator John Cornyn in Texas;

and we delve the perverse minds of the Islamic Center of San Diego shooters.

open.spotify.com/episode/4II…

On the show today:

A judge rules in favor of excluding evidence in the Luigi Mangione trial… and Mangione fans are ecstatic;

Thomas Massie is engaged in a knock-down, drag-out primary with a Trump-endorsed Republican;

and the Call Her Daddy lady is happily married and pregnant, unlike all the ladies who took her life advice.

open.spotify.com/episode/2PM…

